4.1 Identify at least 12 operations
Operations describe actions performed by the system, not just its states.
Operation ID	Operation Name	Purpose
OP-01	AcceptDeliveryRequest	Validate and accept a delivery request.
OP-02	CalculateDeliveryRoute	Select a safe route to the destination.
OP-03	DetectAndAvoidObstacle	Detect an obstacle and plan a safe avoidance manoeuvre.
OP-04	MonitorAndCorrectChamberConditions	Monitor and correct temperature and humidity.
OP-05	DeliverMedicineBatch	Release the medicine batch at the destination under safe conditions.
OP-06	VerifyDeliveryCompletion	Confirm that delivery has actually completed.
OP-07	ReturnToWarehouse	Navigate back to the warehouse.
OP-08	PerformChamberSelfCheck	Check that essential chamber sensors work at startup.
OP-09	LoadBatchProfile	Load batch identity and required environmental limits.
OP-10	AuthenticateAndAuthoriseCommand	Verify the operator's identity and permissions.
OP-11	ActivateSafeMode	Enter the appropriate safety-protection condition.
OP-12	ManageRobotConnections	Manage simultaneous connections to the robot fleet.
OP-13	AuthoriseRailwayCrossingEntry	Check crossing safety conditions before entry.
OP-14	HandleCommunicationLoss	Detect link loss and apply the approved safe policy.
OP-15	RecordAndReportEvent	Record events and report status to Mission Control.
4.2 Operation schemas
OP-08: PerformChamberSelfCheck
- Description: Checks the essential chamber sensors when the system powers on.
- Inputs: Power-on signal, sensor readings.
- Outputs: Self-check result.
- Reads: Temperature, humidity, vibration, door and power sensor status.
- Changes: Marks the self-check as passed or failed.
- Sends/Alerts: Reports sensor failure to Mission Control.
- Assumes (precondition): Chamber power is available.
- Result (postcondition): Monitoring begins only if all essential sensors work; otherwise, normal monitoring is blocked and a fault is reported.
OP-09: LoadBatchProfile
- Description: Loads the identification and environmental requirements of a medicine batch.
- Inputs: Batch ID, temperature limits, humidity limits.
- Outputs: Validated batch profile.
- Reads: Batch identification and configured limits.
- Changes: Stores the active batch profile.
- Sends/Alerts: Reports invalid or missing profile information.
- Assumes (precondition): Batch identification information is available.
- Result (postcondition): A valid profile is stored and ready for use.
OP-04: MonitorAndCorrectChamberConditions
- Description: Monitors chamber temperature and humidity and attempts correction when values fall outside their allowed ranges.
- Inputs: Current readings, target limits, correction command.
- Outputs: Updated sensor readings and correction status.
- Reads: Temperature, humidity, sensor health and batch profile.
- Changes: Activates or adjusts the relevant environmental control.
- Sends/Alerts: Alerts the operator if correction fails within the recovery period.
- Assumes (precondition): Self-check passed, a valid batch profile is loaded, and the chamber door is closed.
- Result (postcondition): Correction is considered successful only after sensor readings confirm that both values are back within range. Otherwise, protection mode is activated.
OP-10: AuthenticateAndAuthoriseCommand
- Description: Checks the identity and permissions of an operator before accepting a robot command.
- Inputs: Credentials, operator role, requested command.
- Outputs: Accept or reject decision.
- Reads: Authentication records, role permissions and command details.
- Changes: Records the command decision and its audit information.
- Sends/Alerts: Reports unauthorised attempts according to the security policy.
- Assumes (precondition): A command and operator identity are supplied.
- Result (postcondition): The command is accepted only if authentication and role authorisation both succeed.
OP-11: ActivateSafeMode
- Description: Protects the robot and medicine when a critical battery, temperature or other safety fault occurs.
- Inputs: Fault type, battery level, temperature reading.
- Outputs: Safe Mode status and fault response.
- Reads: Battery, chamber sensors, current robot state and fault thresholds.
- Changes: Changes the robot to SAFE_MODE and inhibits unsafe actions.
- Sends/Alerts: Sends an urgent fault notification and records the event.
- Assumes (precondition): A critical condition has been detected by a functioning monitoring mechanism.
- Result (postcondition): Safe Mode is entered within 3 seconds for the CR-01 trigger conditions, and unsafe delivery actions are inhibited.
OP-13: AuthoriseRailwayCrossingEntry
- Description: Checks whether it is safe for the robot to enter a railway crossing.
- Inputs: Barrier status, train detection, approach status, sensor health, ARLCCS status.
- Outputs: Entry authorised or denied.
- Reads: Train sensors, barrier sensors, warning signals and communication status.
- Changes: Records the crossing decision; the robot proceeds only when permitted.
- Sends/Alerts: Denies entry and raises an alert when conditions are unsafe or uncertain.
- Assumes (precondition): The robot is approaching the crossing and safety data is available.
- Result (postcondition): Entry is authorised only when the barrier is open, no train is approaching, and the relevant safety inputs are valid.
4.3 How operations change the chamber and robot states
Operation	Initial condition	Action	Resulting state or condition
OP-04: MonitorAndCorrectChamberConditions	Chamber monitoring	Temperature or humidity becomes out of range and correction fails.	Chamber enters protection mode; operator is alerted.
Door-open handling	Active conservation	Door sensor reports that the door has opened.	Normal conservation is suspended until the door is closed and conditions and sensors are verified.
OP-11: ActivateSafeMode	NAVIGATING	Critical battery or temperature condition occurs.	Robot enters SAFE_MODE.
OP-14: HandleCommunicationLoss	NAVIGATING	Control-link timeout occurs.	Robot enters LINK_LOST handling and applies the local safety policy.
The chamber protection mode is a chamber operating condition and should not automatically be treated as identical to the robot's SAFE_MODE state. The robot and chamber exchange fault information, and the robot's state changes according to the system safety policy.
4.4 Operations requiring sensor verification
1. MonitorAndCorrectChamberConditions
Issuing a cooling or humidity-correction command does not prove that the required environmental conditions have been restored. The controller must read the sensors again and verify that the values remain within the batch limits.
2. VerifyDeliveryCompletion
Sending a delivery-complete command does not prove that the package was physically delivered. The system should check appropriate evidence, such as package-release confirmation or a delivery sensor, before recording completion.
A similar rule applies to railway barriers: issuing an open command is not proof that the barrier is physically open. The system must verify barrier feedback.
